course: dictionary
lesson: 1784
title: Clinic: a place to get help
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A clinic is a place where people go to see a doctor, nurse or other health worker. You usually go in and come home the same day, without staying overnight.
explain: «A plaster cast that gets soaked goes soft and weak, so the fracture clinic should be phoned.» The words fracture clinic tell you what kind of clinic it is: one for broken bones. Look at the words next to clinic to work out which kind it is.
explain: A clinic can also be a short session where experts give advice or teach skills, such as a football clinic. Read the sentence around the word to find out which meaning fits.
fact: A clinic is a place where people see a doctor, nurse or health worker.
fact: Most clinic visits are short, so you do not stay overnight.
fact: A clinic can also be a session where experts teach skills, such as a football clinic.
fact: Useful phrases: «a dental clinic», «a health clinic», «a walk-in clinic», «a clinic appointment».
fact: Pets can go to a vet's clinic too.
exercise: Where do people go to see a nurse for a check-up? | At a bakery | At a library | *At a clinic | At a cinema
exercise: «...so the fracture clinic should be phoned.» What kind of clinic is a fracture clinic? | A clinic for football skills | *A clinic for broken bones | A clinic for teeth | A clinic for pets
exercise: A football clinic gives players tips from coaches. What is a clinic here? | A hospital with beds for the night | *A session where experts teach skills | A kind of ball game | A shop that sells boots
test: Sam goes to the dental clinic to have his teeth checked. Where does Sam go? | To the shops for sweets | To a school for maths | To the swimming pool | *To a place where a dentist checks teeth
test: Jade says she has a clinic appointment tomorrow. What does that mean? | Her football team is playing a match | She is teaching a class | *She has a time booked to see a health worker | She is staying in hospital overnight
exam: Which sentence uses clinic in its health meaning? | *Ana went to the clinic to have her jab from the nurse | The clinic was a sunny beach with soft, golden sand | The clinic was a long grey road with lots of cars | Ben rode his clinic to school and rang its bell
